---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — **파는 자료 한 벌의 착륙 지면.** (/data)
 *
 * ── 왜 만드나 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * 2026-08-08 04:3x. 2번 지시로 손님 걸음을 끝까지 걸어 보다 **길 끝이 막힌 것**을 봤다.
 * 「첫 화면 → 목록 → 기사 → 나가는 길 → 한 벌(유료)」에서 마지막 칸이 **없었다.**
 * 한 벌은 `docs/상품안/본보기-한벌/` 에만 있고 손님이 닿을 주소가 하나도 없었다.
 * 사장님 지시 6번 — 「어떤 메뉴도 클릭이 돼야 하고 랜딩페이지가 있어야 한다」.
 *
 * ── ⛔ 이 지면이 하지 않는 것 ─────────────────────────────────
 * ① **값을 안 적는다.** 사장님 판단이고 아직 안 나왔다. 한 벌 검사가 값이 적히면 선다.
 * ② **파일을 안 내려준다.** 넷플릭스 주간 순위의 재배포 조건이 라이선스 대장에 **⬜ 미확인**이다.
 *    확인 전에 파일을 여는 것은 「받기 전에 본다」를 어기는 것이다. 확인되면 그때 연다.
 * ③ 광고 자리를 안 만든다(Riot Production 승인 전).
 *
 * ⚠ 줄 수는 **실제 파일에서 센다.** 손으로 적으면 자료가 움직여도 지면은 안 움직인다.
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import KcwRelatedArticles from '../../components/KcwRelatedArticles.astro';
import titles from '../../data/wikitip-titles.json';
import korea from '../../data/wikitip-korea-signal.json';
import invisible from '../../data/wikitip-kpop-invisible.json';
import { 한벌 } from '../../data/wikitip-bundle';
import { ONE_OFF_USD, MONTHLY_USD, WHY as PRICE_WHY, usd, 여는달 } from '../../data/wikitip-price';

/** 갈래를 열쇠로 찾아 쓴다. 순서가 바뀌어도 안 어긋난다 */
const 안보임 = Object.fromEntries(invisible.rows.map((r) => [r.key, r]));

/* ⛔ 표 목록과 줄 세기는 이제 한 곳에서만 온다. /subscribe 와 다른 수를 말하던 것을 고쳤다. */
const 벌 = 한벌();
const 있는표 = 벌.표;
const 전체줄 = 벌.rows;

/**
 * 파는 것이 **무엇이 들어 있나**를 수로 적는다. (2번 지시 12:3x)
 * ⛔ 손으로 안 적는다 — 파일에서 센다. 자료가 늘면 지면이 저절로 따라간다.
 * ⛔ 값은 안 적는다. 사장님 손이다. **「미정」이라고도 안 적는다** —
 *    손님이 읽는 것은 「아직 안 정했다」가 아니라 「언제 살 수 있나」다.
 */
const MAIL = 'cs@klifedesign.net';
const 열림알림 = `mailto:${MAIL}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('K Culture Wire — tell me when the data opens')}`;

/** 갱신 주기 — 표마다 **원자료가 나오는 주기**다. 우리가 부지런한 정도가 아니다. */
const 갱신 = 있는표.map((t) => ({ 표: t.이름, 언제: t.갱신 }));

const TITLE = 'The data behind these pages';
const DESC = `Every number on this site comes from ${전체줄.toLocaleString()} rows we built and keep. `
  + 'This is what is in them, what is missing from them, and what we have had to correct.';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: 'K Culture Wire data bundle',
  description: DESC,
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'K Culture Wire' },
  isBasedOn: ['https://www.netflix.com/tudum/top10', 'https://query.wikidata.org', 'https://kosis.kr', 'https://dart.fss.or.kr'],
};
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd} canonical="https://www.kculturewire.com/data">
  <h1>The data behind these pages</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Nothing on this site is written from a press release. Every figure comes out of tables we build and
    keep — <b>{전체줄.toLocaleString()} rows</b> across {있는표.length} files. This page says what is in
    them, and it says what is missing from them before it says anything else.
  </p>

  {/*
    2번 지시 12:3x — 「무엇이 들어 있나를 **숫자로**」. 몇 파일 · 몇 줄 · 어떤 꼴 · 얼마나 자주.
    ⛔ 손으로 안 적는다. 위에서 실제 파일을 세서 온 값이다.
  */}
  <section>
    <h2>What is in it</h2>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table class="spec">
        <tbody>
          <tr><th>Tables</th><td><b>{있는표.length}</b> files, one row per thing counted</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Rows</th><td><b>{전체줄.toLocaleString()}</b> across all of them</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Format</th><td>UTF-8 CSV, plus a column dictionary that says what every column means and what a blank cell means</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Covers</th><td>{titles.weekFrom ?? '2021-07-04'} to {titles.weekTo ?? '2026-07-26'} for the chart tables; the last 30 days for daily attention</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Refreshed</th><td>{갱신.map((g) => g.언제).filter((v, i, a) => a.indexOf(v) === i).join(' · ')}</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Also included</th><td>The corrections record and the coverage file, so you can see what we changed and what is missing before you build on it</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      Per table, the refresh is what the <b>source</b> publishes, not how often we feel like looking:
      {' '}{갱신.map((g) => `${g.표} — ${g.언제}`).join('; ')}.
    </p>
    <ul class="files">
      {있는표.map((t) => (
        <li>
          <div class="head"><b>{t.이름}</b><span>{t.줄.toLocaleString()} rows</span></div>
          <p>{t.말}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Two rulers, not one</h2>
    <p class="body">
      The first question anyone should ask about a panel is what put a row in it. Ours has two answers.
    </p>
    <p class="body">
      <b>The name.</b> Netflix publishes no country of production, so a title enters because its English
      name matches a Korean work in Wikidata. That can fail in exactly one way — another country made
      something with the same name — so we measured how often it can.
      {' '}<b>{korea.sharedTitles} of {titles.titleCount}</b> titles carry a name a foreign work also carries.
    </p>
    <p class="body">
      <b>Korea's own chart.</b> A Korean title normally also plays in Korea, so we counted every title's
      weeks on Netflix's South Korea list. <b>{korea.sharedWithoutKorea} of those {korea.sharedTitles}
      have never appeared on it</b>, and {korea.queues.oneCountryOnly} charted in exactly one country in
      the world. Those columns are in the table, per row, so you can sort by them yourself.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      <b>Neither ruler decides alone and we do not hide the disagreement.</b> A Korean work can miss
      Korea's chart because it was released before this data begins, or was never streamed there.
      Nothing has been removed on the second ruler's strength alone — it produces a queue to read, and
      anything we do remove appears on <a href="/corrections">the corrections page</a> with the evidence.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What is missing</h2>
    <p class="body">
      We would rather you learned this from us than from a spreadsheet at six in the evening.
    </p>
    <ul class="gaps">
      <li><b>Hours per country.</b> Netflix publishes viewing hours for its global list only. The country lists carry rank and nothing else, and no source we can reach fills this.</li>
      <li><b>What sits below each weekly top ten.</b> Unpublished, so we cannot even count what is missing.</li>
      <li><b>Cast completeness.</b> Wikidata's cast lists are short and skew to well-known names. Every network figure we publish is a floor, not a count.</li>
      <li>
        <b>Acts with no English Wikipedia article.</b> They produce no row in the attention panel.
        We counted how many: Wikidata holds <b>{안보임.groups.all.toLocaleString()}</b> Korean musical
        groups and we measure the <b>{안보임.groups.withEn.toLocaleString()}</b> with an English
        article, so <b>{안보임.groups.missing.toLocaleString()} ({안보임.groups.missingPc}%)</b> are
        outside it. Among singers it is {안보임.singer.missing.toLocaleString()} of{' '}
        {안보임.singer.all.toLocaleString()} ({안보임.singer.missingPc}%), and{' '}
        {안보임.singer.koNotEn.toLocaleString()} of those have a Korean article.
        {' '}<a href="/article/the-acts-our-k-pop-panel-cannot-see">How we counted it →</a>
        <div class="prov">
          {invisible.method}{' '}
          {invisible.limit}{' '}
          {invisible.overlapWarning}{' '}
          Counted across {invisible.queriedGroups + invisible.failedGroups} Wikidata queries
          {invisible.failedGroups > 0
            ? `, of which ${invisible.failedGroups} returned no answer and are recorded as empty rather than zero`
            : ', all of which answered'}.
          Occupations are <code>{invisible.occupations.join(' ')}</code>, the same codes the
          attention panel is built from.
        </div>
      </li>
      <li><b>Export figures for 2025 and 2026.</b> The survey runs about eighteen months behind.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="note">
      The same list is in <code>coverage.csv</code> in a form you can filter, with a column saying
      whether each gap can ever be filled.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="ask">
    <h2>How to get it</h2>
    <p class="body">
      <b>Email <a href="mailto:cs@klifedesign.net?subject=K%20Culture%20Wire%20data">cs@klifedesign.net</a></b>{' '}
      and say what you are trying to answer. We will tell you whether these tables can answer it —
      including when they cannot, which is the more useful reply.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      {/*
        ⛔ 2026-08-08 07:5x. 사는 데까지 걸어 보니 **언제 답하는지**를 말한 적이 없었다.
           손님은 메일을 보내고 나서 기다릴지 딴 데를 볼지 정해야 한다. 그 판단을 못 하게 두고 있었다.
      */}
      <b>What happens then.</b> We reply within one working day, in Korean or English, with a plain
      answer to whether these tables cover your question. If they do, you get the files and the column
      dictionary; if they do not, we say what would have to exist and we do not sell you the near miss.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      {/*
        ⛔ 08:0x. 넷플릭스 없는 한 벌을 07시에 만들어 놓고 **이 지면이 그것을 몰랐다.**
           오늘 바로 건넬 수 있는 것이 손님에게 안 보이는 채로 있었다.
      */}
      <b>Two of these panels are ready to hand over today.</b> The K-pop attention table and the listed
      company table rest only on Wikimedia, Wikidata, KOSIS and Korea's corporate filings, and we have
      checked those terms. They are bundled separately for exactly that reason, with the corrections
      record alongside them, and nothing in that bundle is derived from a streaming chart.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      {/*
        값이 정해졌다 (2번 15:5x · 사장님이 우리에게 맡기셨다).
        ⛔ 값을 여기 손으로 안 적는다. `wikitip-price.ts` 한 곳에서만 온다 —
           지면마다 적으면 바꿀 때 한쪽만 고쳐진다. 오늘 아침 한 벌 크기에서 그 병을 겪었다.
        ⛔ 넷플릭스 없는 한 벌은 값을 **안 지어낸다.** 재배포 조건이 아직 ⬜ 미확인이다.
      */}
      <b>{usd(ONE_OFF_USD)}</b> for the bundle as it stands, or <b>{usd(MONTHLY_USD)} a month</b> for
      the refreshes and whatever tables we add. One licence covers one organisation —{' '}
      <a href="/terms"> the terms are short</a>.
      <br /><br />
      <b>The opening month is free.</b> Everything above is open at no charge from {여는달()}. That is
      the full price standing with the month opened, not a discount — we would rather you saw what it
      costs and then decided.
      <br /><br />
      <b>Why that price.</b> {PRICE_WHY[0]} {PRICE_WHY[1]}
      <br /><br />
      <b>One table is waiting on someone else.</b> We are not offering the chart-derived tables as a
      public download yet: the redistribution terms for that source are still being confirmed, and we
      check a licence before we publish, not after. The other tables do not wait on it, and the
      Netflix-free bundle is <b>priced separately</b> once we know what we are allowed to include.
    </p>
  </section>

  <KcwRelatedArticles page="/data" />

  <p class="back"><a href="/">&larr; Back to the front page</a></p>
</WikiTip>

<style>
  h1 { font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 5vw, 2.4rem); line-height: 1.25; margin: 1.2rem 0 .8rem; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
  .lead { font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 2.5rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  section { margin: 0 0 3rem; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.12rem; margin: 0 0 .6rem; letter-spacing: -.01em; }
  .body { font-size: .92rem; line-height: 1.75; margin: 0 0 .9rem; }
  .note { font-size: .84rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.7; margin: .9rem 0 0; }

  .files { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
  .files li { padding: .9rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .files .head { display: flex; gap: .8rem; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; }
  .files b { font-size: 1rem; }
  .files .head span { font-size: .82rem; color: var(--accent); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; white-space: nowrap; }
  .files p { font-size: .87rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.65; margin: .3rem 0 0; }

  .spec { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: .88rem; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .spec th { text-align: left; padding: .5rem .8rem .5rem 0; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600;
             white-space: nowrap; vertical-align: top; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .spec td { padding: .5rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); line-height: 1.6; }

  .gaps { padding-left: 1.1rem; margin: 0; font-size: .89rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  .gaps li { margin: 0 0 .5rem; }
  .prov { margin: .45rem 0 0; font-size: .8rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.6; }
  .prov code { font-size: .95em; }

  .ask { background: var(--card); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.2rem 1.1rem; }
  .ask h2 { margin-top: 0; }
  code { font-size: .85em; }
  .back { margin-top: 3rem; font-size: .9rem; }
  .back a { color: var(--muted); }
</style>
